From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Dolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:58:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: apple: Add the T8132 compatibles the Mac mini
 boots with

The M4 (T8132) Mac mini needs its NVMe controller, the SART, the SMC,
the SPMI controllers, the PCIe controller and their DARTs and mailboxes
before it can boot from its SSD and reach the network. Each block works
with an existing generation's driver, so add the T8132 compatibles with
the fallbacks T8122 and T8140 already use:

- apple,t8132-dart        (apple,t8110-dart)
- apple,t8132-sart        (apple,t6000-sart)
- apple,t8132-asc-mailbox (apple,asc-mailbox-v4)
- apple,t8132-smc         (apple,t8103-smc)
- apple,t8132-spmi        (apple,t8103-spmi)
- apple,t8132-pcie        (apple,t6020-pcie), next to apple,t8122-pcie
- apple,abbey-pmic        (apple,spmi-nvmem), the T8132 main PMU

A J773g runs today with these compatibles and fallbacks under
GravityLinux's gravity-m4 kernel. The DART and mailbox lines are the
same as in the open omacom/linux-aurora #200 (T8132 SEP); whichever
change lands second drops them.

Signed-off-by: Sean Dolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
